==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Furilan Pasalan''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Ragelan Pasalan''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
This form is <u>useless by design</u>. Similar to the other cats from Tales of the Nekoluga, this cat is not meant to be used until it evolves.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Intentionally or otherwise, Furilan Pasalan is <u>borderline useless</u> against anything that doesn't have a [[Shield]]. Due to its abysmal stats and lack of general abilities, the only reason to use Furilan Pasalan is to safely and reliably break the Shields of major enemies such as [[Le'Behemoth]] and [[Fallen Bear]], as its range exceeds that of any other [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercer]]. While it does do a good job at breaking Shields and [[Barrier]]s once every 18 seconds, if you just want to break Barriers and not Shields, the [[Ototo Corps|Breakerblast Cannon]] could save you a slot. Even setting the Breakerblast aside, several non-Uber units can break Barriers like Furilan Pasalan while being cheaper to deploy and/or providing literally anything more aside from just breaking Barriers.

It is also worth mentioning that although Furilan Pasalan has extremely long range, it is very much vulnerable to [[Surge Attack]]s. This is especially dangerous against Fallen Bears and [[Condemned Peng]]s, as these enemies' surges can take out Furilan very easily if they reach it, and they very consistently surge as they are spawned and sometimes spammed often in [[The Aku Realms]]. Without the protection of [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] or [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]], surges from [[Sinner Snache]] may also break the Cat frontline and leave Furiluga defenseless.

==='''True Form'''===
Ragelan Pasalan gains more health, a faster attack rate and Surge Immunity. It still carries most of its previous flaws, primarily its low survivability and long cooldown while being outclassed at countering Barriers, but is now a safer pick in Aku stages by easily dismissing two of their major gimmicks. Additionally, surge-immune defenders such as [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]] can improve its survivability further by keeping Aku enemies from pushing.

As expected, Ragelan Pasalan's 100% Mini-Surge can be inconsistent, as its nature as an anti-Shield specialist means it doesn't serve to inflict extra damage. However, since Shield Piercing isn't reliant on the unit's own damage and the Surge has a tiny spawn area, Ragelan Pasalan can potentially snipe and destroy Shields that are just outside of its attack range by catching those that wander into its area of effect, saving other units a lot of trouble.

Finally, Ragelan Pasalan gains a [[Cat Combo]] with [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] that boosts Worker Start Level by 2. Being rather efficient for its effect, it helps to greatly ease awkward startoffs in many Aku stages, as both units specialize in demolishing enemy Shields. Additionally, it could potentially be paired with the likes of [[Longnecks (Combo)|Longnecks]], [[Don't Mess With Me! (Combo)|Don't Mess With Me!]], [[Cat Transport (Combo)|Cat Transport]] and [[Itchy Riches (Combo)|Itchy Riches]]. As such, this True Form may be worth it even if just for the combo.

==='''Talents'''===
Ragelan Pasalan requires a massive investment for his talents, but they certainly improve him significantly.

'''[[Strengthen]]''' and '''[[Survive]]''' are practically only useful in tandem, as the former only activates when Ragelan is at 1% HP, which is obviously too much for a unit with only 1 knockback to handle. Survive is guaranteed to activate when maxed, while a fully upgraded Strengthen talent boosts his damage by a massive 500%. Although difficult to activate, it turns Ragelan's not-so-great damage into an extremely destructive force—disregarding other talents, a level 50 Ragelan can deal a massive 194k damage per hit at a whopping 700 range, and if the attack knocks the target into his Mini-Surge it gets bumped up to 272k damage per attack cycle. This drastically expands Ragelan's utility from a ranged anti-Shield unit to a powerful DPS backliner.

'''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Wave Resist]]''' isn't noteworthy despite the existence of Wave Resist Orbs, as they are only useful at S-grade (anything less will still deal damage and destroy Ragelan after it activates its Survive ability). Obtaining an entire S-grade Resist Orb for this particular unit is not recommended, although it does let him reliably counter [[Deathkory]] and [[Wicked Face]].

Finally, '''HP Up''' should not be considered under any circumstance, as Ragelan has poor survivability. '''Attack Up''' is good for bolstering Ragelan's new role as a nuker, but it's only necessary to get the last bit of damage out of Ragelan after boosting with Catseyes.

==='''Orb'''===
Since Ragelan Pasalan technically doesn't target any traits and is used as a general DPS backliner when talented, it can be theoretically paired with any Attack Up Orb. As mentioned before, players who wish to capitalize on its Wave Resist talent can also choose to equip an S-grade Wave Resist Orb, which improves its matchups against Wave threats and removes another way of reaching it in the back.

