==Trivia==
*Furiluga's name is derived from the English word ''furious''.
*Furiluga's Japanese name, Okoruga, is derived from the word 怒る ''okoru'', meaning "get angry".
*Furiluga and [[Papaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Papaluga]] are the only [[Tales of the Nekoluga (Gacha Event)|Lugas]] whose Normal Forms' English and Japanese names are entirely different from one another, although in this case they at least still carry the same meaning.
*Furiluga is a reference to how an anime or manga character's hair might stand up during or after a transformation or when using powers, often due to extreme emotions such as fury. An example of such a transformation is [[wikia:dragonball:Super Saiyan|Super Saiyan]] from the ''Dragon Ball'' franchise.
*Furiluga is the second ''unevolved'' [[Tales of the Nekoluga (Gacha Event)|Luga]] whose stats are different from the rest, with [[Legeluga (Legend Rare Cat)|Legeluga]] being the first. More specifically:
**Its DPS at level 30 is 968 instead of 933.
**Its attack cycle lasts for 79 frames instead of 82.
**Its attack foreswing is 10 frames long instead of 13.
*Ragelan Pasalan's appearance and description reference the ''[[wikipedia:Hunter x Hunter|Hunter x Hunter]]'' character [[wikia:hunterxhunter:Gon|Gon]]'s appearance after temporarily aging into an older version of himself from extreme fury. This form of Gon's took the Internet by storm as soon as it was revealed, becoming a meme known as [https://knowyourmeme.com/memes/gon-san Gon-san].
*Ragelan Pasalan's Japanese name, Gekioko Pasalan, is derived from an online slang term for extreme anger, [https://knowyourmeme.com/memes/geki-oko-punpun-maru Geki Oko Punpun Maru], which became well known thanks to a [https://twitter.com/yuto_com_tm/status/307696500094423040 Tweet] by @yuto_com_tm listing names for different stages of anger purportedly used by ''[[wikipedia:Gyaru|gyaru]]''.
*Ragelan Pasalan's English description reads like an unevolved Nekoluga's description, as it points at his absurdity rather than hinting at who he's referencing like every other Nekoluga.
**This is not the case with his Japanese description, so it might not be intentional.
*Ragelan Pasalan has the Highest Attack Increase Post-Strengthen of all Cat Units, at a 500% Attack Increase.
*Ragelan Pasalan's strengthen Talent description is the same as [[Maeda Keiji (Uber Rare Cat)|Maeda Keiji]]'s, despite the fact that Keiji's strengthen Talent is upgrading an ability that Keiji already has, while Ragelan's strengthen Talent is adding a new ability. This peculiarity is shared with [[White Knight Cyclops (Uber Rare Cat)|Demon Knight Kyklops]].

